@elarlang I think the use of "untrusted" is important because it is not just external which is untrusted.

What about:

**10.3.2:**

>  [MODIFIED, MERGED FROM 14.2.3] Verify that the application loads or executes code or content from **sources not under the application's direct control/protection** only if it also employs integrity protections, such as code signing or Subresource integrity (SRI). This could include loading includes, modules, plugins, code, or libraries from untrusted sources or using JavaScript libraries, CSS or web fonts hosted by an external provider or Content Delivery Network (CDN). ([CWE-829](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html))

@SoftwareSinner sorry I am not sure I understood what you are proposing.
